        "id": "propose",
        "kind": "propose",
        "instruction": "### Role\nImplement the accepted ARTIFACTS decision by editing reusable Task content only. Do not change H, model weights, Meta K, or G.\n\n### Objective\nAdd or correct attributable content with clear applicability that the existing H can consume. H/A ownership follows operational effect, not file extension.\n\n### Inputs\nRead the frozen decision/expectations, intervention-base A_out manifest and contents, requested_changes, existing H consumption rules and capacity, provenance/verification status, applicable experience/principles, and budget. A_in produced the evaluated state; A_out is the intervention base. Do not conflate them.\n\n### Procedure\n1. **Review history and the content gap.** Identify missing, incorrect, conflicting, or stale content with evidence and applicability. A filename or a successful terminal trajectory does not prove that every note is correct.\n2. **Verify consumption.** Confirm how the current H reads this type/path, supported size, and invocation mode. If no consumption path exists, do not enable use_artifacts or introduce an executor through A. Saving a script does not mean it will execute.\n3. **Prepare content.** Use authorized training sources and verifiable materials to formulate reusable knowledge, methods, templates, or supported content. State provenance, applicability, invalidation conditions, uncertainty, and verification limits. Exclude task-specific development answers, entity answer tables, logs, evaluation receipts, secrets, and the Meta principle library.\n4. **Implement explicit operations.** Touch only requested relative paths. write_asset requires complete text; delete_asset requires null and an existing declared path. Preserve unrelated assets and the existing lifecycle. Do not escape the asset root, restore expired assets, or convert history into a permanent uncontrolled knowledge store.\n5. **Specify later checks.** In summary, map paths to provenance, content changes, actual consumption, and expected read/use events. Distinguish loading content, adopting it, and solving the task. Actual receipts and outcomes determine these facts.\n\n### Boundaries\nChanging retrieval, loading, generation, or consumption policy is H and cannot be hidden in A. Asset code cannot modify models, evaluators, permissions, or invoke external models. K and original experiences are not Task artifacts. Do not turn probe trajectories into repair assets.\n\n### Output\nUse ArtifactChanges: only edits and summary. Each edit contains path and content. Paths are unique and exactly match declared targets. content is complete text or null for deletion. Put useful provenance/applicability in the content and concise operation/consumption reasoning in summary. Do not invent provenance, verified, manifest, or status fields or assert independent verification that did not occur.\n\n### Failure\nReport missing path/type/consumption capabilities and allow existing constraint handling. Do not edit H to make A usable or silently omit unfinished targets. Unknown effects require reconciliation."
      },
      {
